From: Jonathan Barnes <hello@jonbarnes.dev>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:14:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Dust floats in the light and not in the shadow

Patch 0035 of the renderer series (OoT: Recompiled).

The user, 2026-10-08, looking up at the Temple of Time's tall window: "maybe just have particle
ambience throughout the air that would cause this kind of ... thing. And in the shadows, the
particles are not shown. So, like, really, really subtle particles that float through light areas
only".

The air pass now also looks for motes of dust along the eye's ray, as far as the surface it sees
and no more than a thousand units: one mote at most in each forty unit cell of a grid, placed and
kept by a hash of the cell, drifting slowly about its place. A mote the ray passes shows as a soft
speck one to three pixels across, lit by the light that actually reaches it, each light followed
by a shadow ray: a window's or a shaft's light, the sun's under a sky, the game's own lights within
their reach. In shadow a mote is not there at all. The shadow rays are spent only on motes the ray
passes, a few pixels in a hundred.

A new configuration value, the Dust in the light row (0 to 1, in the reflections' last spare
slot), sets how bright; 0 turns it off and is the default.

diff --git a/src/render/rt64_raytracing_resources.cpp b/src/render/rt64_raytracing_resources.cpp
--- a/src/render/rt64_raytracing_resources.cpp
+++ b/src/render/rt64_raytracing_resources.cpp
